int for fo~ty· three years and sighing for eighty-one, "r. t." entered into the enJoyrnent of the great salvation. May the glorious gospel of the blessed God produce in us a greater cheerfulness than this epitaph displays ; but may this be attended by a humility as true if not as sad. What a blessing that sorrowing and sighing saints are safe in the arms of Jesus I Might they not for this very reason change sighing into singing? lsAAo NEAR,

